+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Loading anchors, aliases and merge keys
+
+- [x] 1.1 In `tree.py`, add `Anchor` (name, start, end) on `Node` and `Alias` (name, start, end, target) on `Entry` and `Item`. Move `node.start` past the anchor, and any whitespace, comments, line breaks and tag after it. Make an alias's `value` the anchored `Node` object, keeping `anchors: dict[str, Node]` filled on completion. Raise `LoadError` (naming the file) for an undefined alias, an alias inside its own anchor, and an anchored or alias key (D1). Verify that `uv run mypy` is clean and that the existing `uv run pytest` suite passes except `test_anchors_are_refused_at_load`
+- [x] 1.2 In `tree.py`, resolve plain untagged `<<` keys at mapping end into a resolved `MappingNode`, with `written` holding the mapping as written. Merged entries take the `<<` position, in source order, with local keys and earlier sources winning. A merge value that is not a mapping or a list of mappings (an include string included) fails to load (D3). Verify with the tests in 1.4
+- [x] 1.3 In `loader.py`, memoise `_Loader.expand` by node identity so that an anchored node (including an anchored include string) is expanded once and shared by its aliases. In `overrides.merge`, carry `alias` onto the `Entry` objects it creates (D2). Verify with a test that `a: &x file:inc.yaml\nb: *x\n` loads, reads `inc.yaml` once and gives both paths the same values
+- [x] 1.4 Replace `test_anchors_are_refused_at_load` with `tests/test_aliases_loading.py`, run through the real CLI, covering every "Anchors, aliases and merge keys" scenario: mapping alias, scalar alias, merge key, list of merges, quoted `"<<"`, import events at every aliased path, undefined alias, anchors not crossing files, alias inside its own anchor, scalar merge value. Add `show --sources` naming the anchor's file for an aliased value, and a reconcile test where a hand edit at the anchor records events for every aliased path. Verify they pass and that the merge-order test fails if local keys stop winning
+- [x] 1.5 Update README: replace decision 8 with the loading rules (anchors, aliases, merge keys; what still fails with exit 4) and list it in the exit-code table's code-4 row. Verify the README example config with an anchor loads with `uv run troupe config show --theatre /tmp/demo`
+
+## 2. Setting values defined at an anchor
